{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "1) Evidence: We have only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), which establishes a weak RNA baseline. The most critical unknown is whether the image modality carries useful signal at all, since the entire multimodal branch of the search space depends on this. 2) This experiment tests image-only (resnet50, singleprofile) as a clean, single-variable comparison to the RNA-only baseline, isolating the contribution of the image modality without confounding with encoder choice, aggregation, or fusion. 3) Under a 10-experiment budget, resolving whether image is a strong or weak signal is the highest-value uncertainty to reduce early: if image performs comparably or better than RNA, we can confidently invest remaining experiments in multimodal fusion; if it is substantially weaker, we can redirect budget toward improving RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. ResNet50 is chosen as the standard, well-calibrated image encoder to give an unbiased first read on image signal."
}

